from pathlib import Path
updates={
'ARCHITECTURE.md':'''\n## ARE-A3.1 validation hardening (unreleased source candidate)\n\nInitialization validates schema v1 within its existing transaction before accepting an\nexisting database; explicit validate_database uses a read transaction and the same private\nvalidator. The packaged schema remains the authority. All seven required tables, ordered\ncolumns, types, nullability, primary/unique keys, foreign keys, positive-revision CHECKs and\nautoincrement definition are checked. Supported table definitions must match packaged v1\nafter cosmetic SQL normalization; alternative equivalent DDL is not certified. Extra\nunrelated tables/indexes/triggers are allowed. Ten immutable triggers must retain their\nexpected table, event, timing and unconditional abort body; names alone do not suffice.\n\nThe single version-1 migration entry needs a timezone-bearing timestamp and the packaged\nchecksum. Stored descriptor/revision/review JSON and typed contracts, digests, historical\nrights references and review-state/history consistency are checked. Stale assignments may\nreference historical rights revisions and remain valid databases. No schema or migration\nchanges, automatic repair, reset or external host operation are introduced.\n''',
'CONTRACTS.md':'''\n## ARE-A3.1 persisted-database validation\n\nPublic signatures, schema version 1 and successful validate_database() response\n{"valid": True, "schema_version": 1} remain unchanged. Invalid supported-schema structures,\nledger metadata or stored JSON/contracts/references raise existing DomainError with code\nVALIDATION and table/row diagnostics. SQLite failures retain code DATABASE. Malformed\npersisted JSON and missing migration rows never escape as raw parsing/indexing exceptions.\nValidation rejects the input transaction without repairing or discarding records.\n\nValidation is performed at construction and on explicit request, not before every call\non an already constructed instance. The trusted custodian must prevent external changes\nduring operations and quarantine rejected restores. This is an unreleased source candidate;\naccepted 1.0.0/1.1.0 wheel behavior and historical reports remain unchanged.\n''',
'SECURITY.md':'''\n## ARE-A3.1 validation limits\n\nThe unreleased source candidate checks complete required schema definitions and critical\ntrigger bodies, migration identity and stored contract/reference consistency. This detects\nmissing schema objects and obvious same-name no-op/conditional trigger replacements.\nChecks use reads and roll back on failure; invalid storage is not repaired or migrated.\n\nThese diagnostics do not establish reviewer identity, rights authenticity, storage scope\nor protection against administrators who edit SQLite, the validator or package together.\nSelf-consistent forged data or substituted databases can still pass. Extra schema objects\nare not security-certified. Custody, authentication, authorization, host reservations,\ndurable receipts and external audit remain production prerequisites (A3 G01–G07).\n''',
'CHANGELOG.md':'''\n## Unreleased — ARE-A3.1 database validation hardening\n\n- Normalize invalid migration ledger/metadata and malformed stored JSON/contracts into\n  existing DomainError; preserve invalid database bytes without repair.\n- Validate all required schema-v1 tables/columns/constraints and critical trigger bodies,\n  digests and historical revision/review references. Public APIs and schema remain v1.\n- Add disposable-database regression coverage and correct README base-version label.\n- Accepted 1.0.0/1.1.0 wheels and historical acceptance reports remain frozen.\n'''}
for name,addition in updates.items():
 p=Path(name);p.write_bytes(p.read_bytes()+addition.encode())
p=Path('README.md'); b=p.read_bytes().replace(b'ARE-A1',b'ARE-A3.1',1).replace(b'version 1.0.0',b'base version 1.1.0 (unreleased hardening)',1)
b=b.replace(b'.venv-a2\\Scripts\\python scripts/verify_release.py\r\n',b'').replace(b'.venv-a2\\Scripts\\python scripts/verify_release.py\n',b'')
b=b.replace(b'--wheel-dir dist',b'--wheel-dir verification/a3_1/candidate')
p.write_bytes(b)
with p.open('ab') as f: f.write('''\n## ARE-A3.1 source validation\n\nThe accepted wheels retain their original behavior. The hardening is an unreleased source\ncandidate based on 1.1.0; installing the accepted wheel does not install these repairs.\nThe accepted-wheel verification commands above describe the original release; its full\ndiscovery command now includes new regressions that deliberately fail on that release.\nUse the source for the current verification (PowerShell, component directory):\n\n```powershell\n$env:PYTHONPATH=(Resolve-Path src).Path\npython -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_database_validation.py -v\npython -B -m unittest discover -s tests -v\npython -B scripts/test_offline.py\nRemove-Item Env:\\PYTHONPATH -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n```\n\nStartup and explicit validation reject incomplete migration metadata, malformed stored\nJSON/contracts, missing required tables/columns/constraints, weakened critical triggers\nand inconsistent stored references using DomainError. They do not repair data. Schema v1,\npublic APIs and valid snapshots remain compatible. See ARCHITECTURE.md for supported DDL\nand SECURITY.md for limits: database validation is not protection against privileged\nadministrators and does not close the production host prerequisites.\n\nFor diagnostics, validate a completed disposable snapshot in an isolated directory with\n`python scripts/database.py <temporary-copy-directory>` under source PYTHONPATH. Do not\npoint initialization/diagnostic commands at unrelated or production storage.\n`scripts/verify_release.py` is the preserved historical A2 source-baseline verifier and\nis not the acceptance verifier for this changed source. Current evidence is in\n`verification/a3_1/` and `ARE_A3_1_VALIDATION_REPORT.md`.\n'''.encode())
